  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Localized Disaster Risk Reduction and Emergency Preparedness through Effective Stakeholder Coordination.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sri Lanka experiences a range of hazards owing to its geographical proximity just south of the Bay of Bengal and is at risk of heightened impacts of climactic disasters, witnessing an increase in the intensity, frequency and unpredictability of extreme weather events in recent years. Despite the implementation of a range of policy frameworks, strategies and systems to overcome issues related to disaster risk reduction and preparedness, challenges persist in the coordination mechanisms between different development sectors. Through this project, the International Organization for Migration (IOM) contributes towards effective emergency preparedness and localized response mechanisms at divisional and grama niladhari divisions in Sri Lanka, focusing on enhancing the capacity of responsible agencies and communities to respond to disaster-related emergencies and increasing community awareness on emergency response.</narrative>
  </description>
